---
source: crates/agent-compose/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&output)
---
Cancel an execution a `serve` is running, and every open child execution it started (validates, builds, then launches; `--no-build` launches the built tree as it stands)

Usage: agent-compose cancel [OPTIONS] <PATH> <EXECUTION>

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          Path to the spec entrypoint (conventionally `main.yml`)

  <EXECUTION>
          The execution to cancel, as `serve` answered it (`execution_id`)

Options:
      --url <URL>
          The serving app's base URL [default: the target's `hub.public_url`]

      --header <NAME: VALUE>
          One request header, repeatable: the credential the starting trigger's `auth:` reads

      --target <NAME>
          Deploy target to resolve and emit for
          
          [default: local]

      --out <DIR>
          Where to write the generated project [default: <project>/build/<target>]

      --no-build
          Launch the project already built in the output directory as it stands: no validation, no build, and the spec is not read

      --format <FORMAT>
          How to report what was found, and what the app answered

          Possible values:
          - human: Written for a person, on stderr
          - json:  One JSON object on stdout
          
          [default: human]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
